You have to formulate the question differently:

"On average how many donations do I have to make get 1 point of protection."

I did this computation for you in another post but it bears repeating:

EV = (probability of success) * (number of donations)

We want an expected value of 1 so:

1 = PS * ND

So the expected number of donations required to get an average of a point is:

1/PS

Since PS is 1/current protection, the expected number of donations to get the
point is the current protection. So here's my numbers

1st point:  9 donations
2nd point: 10 donations
3rd point: 11 donations
4th point: 12 donations
5th point: 13 donations

Total for 5 points on average: 54 donations. Not 36.3.

Note again it's an average. you could get 5 points on 5 donations. You could
make 700 donations and never get to 5 points. But on average you'd have to
make 54 donations to get those 5 points.

That's $21600 at XL1, which is more than value in the generated shops.

